 //    ]
 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return from one header, defaults to
+no limit. When a header has more valid ranges than `limit` (counted after
+`combine`, if enabled), they are collapsed into a single range from the lowest
+start to the highest end, so the response can be served as a single range
+instead of multipart. Values that are not a number of at least `1` are ignored.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-4,10-14,20-24', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 24 }
+//    ]
+```
+
